# Club & Grub - World 9, stage 2b: "Storm Nest" (designer D9a, Book II "The Far Shore").
# The second half of The Roc's Spire (difficulty 9, Expert only; DESIGN.md A.2 / A.6 / B.5, GAMEPLAY.md 13.6): a
# short approach along the spire top - the Cave Painting (index 15) waits in a hollow under a breakable floor
# blocks - the checkpoint, then a drop of ten rows into the Storm Roc's arena (the boss owner's
# levels/test_enemies_roc.lvl, shifted): a 20 x 11 lock with the stone floor on its last row, the stick nest
# (one-way, arena cols 6-13 row 8) with the Roc perched on it, the floor at row 10 (the runway, wall to wall)
# and the air over both runways free for its storm cruise (G46). Phases 1-2 fall to the club (the head while it
# perches, the buried beak after a dive); in phase 3 the hang-glider appears on the nest by itself: a run-up, a
# climb on lift against a side wall and three dives onto its back while it cruises over one runway half. The Roc
# coughs up the fire-starter over the nest; the exit totem stands locked on the right runway.

